1
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:55,200
Aren't these

2
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:55,900
Changxuan's favorite

3
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:57,120
spring rolls with three fillings?

4
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,780
Yes, Miss.

5
00:01:59,099 --> 00:02:00,819
The three fillings

6
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:02,959
are seasoned with a rich scallop stock.

7
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,560
We put hand-picked

8
00:02:04,659 --> 00:02:06,079
bamboo shoots from the Tianmu Mountain,

9
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,060
plus shredded Xuanwei ham as well as

10
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:10,159
shredded breast from freshly slaughtered chicken.

11
00:02:10,419 --> 00:02:11,199
Just how young master

12
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:12,500
likes them.

13
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:14,300
The freshness of spring

14
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:15,419
is springing in every bite.

15
00:02:15,659 --> 00:02:17,919
Thus the byname— "biting into spring."

16
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,620
It's more than just a lucky name

17
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:20,199
for a happy new year.

18
00:02:20,379 --> 00:02:21,539
Each crisp layer

19
00:02:21,539 --> 00:02:23,560
wraps a little good fortune inside.

20
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:24,919
May your family enjoy

21
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,620
a smooth, happy year ahead.

22
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:30,699
Changxuan hardly ever makes it back home.

23
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,439
He'll miss out again this time.

24
00:02:33,879 --> 00:02:34,680
Indeed.

25
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,620
No one knows if Miss Ye

26
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,599
will ever wake up.

27
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,500
It's been over two years.

28
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,120
What if she never wakes up?

29
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,520
Madam...

30
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,360
You want to take that back!

31
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,419
If anything happened to Pingjun,

32
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:50,020
if she...

33
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:51,199
didn't make it,

34
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:53,780
would Changxuan survive it?

35
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:55,819
I can't sit here.

36
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:00,159
Something doesn't feel right.

37
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,560
I need to go to Redleaf.

38
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:03,659
Mother.

39
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,340
Changxuan's made it clear

40
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:06,580
we are not to disturb them.

41
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:08,620
He must have his reasons.

42
00:03:09,659 --> 00:03:11,979
Let's just keep waiting,

43
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:13,460
lest we made things harder for him.

44
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,199
That's right, Mother.

45
00:03:16,659 --> 00:03:18,680
Changxuan always knows what he's doing.

46
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:20,219
Rest assured.

47
00:03:24,439 --> 00:03:25,080
Go on, eat.

48
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,039
Madam.

49
00:03:42,379 --> 00:03:43,259
It's time for medicine.

50
00:03:49,699 --> 00:03:50,879
I'll take it myself.

51
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,099
There. Easy.

52
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,300
It doesn't seem

53
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,840
as bitter as yesterday's.

54
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,120
Master noticed

55
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,199
you found it bitter,

56
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:17,560
and had us add osmanthus honey.

57
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:19,680
He wrote a note about it

58
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,759
and sent it to the kitchen

59
00:04:20,759 --> 00:04:21,680
in case we forgot.

60
00:04:24,579 --> 00:04:25,399
Madam,

61
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,980
there's something I don't get.

62
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,680
We all think the master's pouring his love

63
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,480
all over you and you alone.

64
00:04:33,579 --> 00:04:34,519
But you never actually

65
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:36,180
seem so happy about it.

66
00:04:40,199 --> 00:04:41,199
Just the fact that

67
00:04:41,839 --> 00:04:43,240
he's stayed by my side,

68
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,639
taking meticulous care of me

69
00:04:45,399 --> 00:04:47,500
all this time I was unconscious,

70
00:04:47,779 --> 00:04:48,800
never giving up on me,

71
00:04:49,439 --> 00:04:50,680
is more than most people

72
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,879
could manage.

73
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,060
The day I woke up,

74
00:04:57,779 --> 00:04:58,879
I saw him there.

75
00:04:59,899 --> 00:05:01,540
I saw the relief in his eyes.

76
00:05:06,939 --> 00:05:07,660
You're awake.

77
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:12,100
That's when I knew

78
00:05:13,379 --> 00:05:14,779
he really does care about me.

79
00:05:17,139 --> 00:05:18,000
But...

80
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,019
But you always seem

81
00:05:20,019 --> 00:05:21,800
to keep him at arm's length.

82
00:05:25,279 --> 00:05:26,779
I know he's decent.

83
00:05:27,839 --> 00:05:29,579
But somehow

84
00:05:30,339 --> 00:05:31,339
I keep feeling like

85
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,740
we will always

86
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,160
travel on completely different paths.

87
00:05:35,879 --> 00:05:37,639
We're from two distinct worlds.

88
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,360
How could we ever end up together?

89
00:05:50,839 --> 00:05:51,699
Mr. Yu,

90
00:05:52,279 --> 00:05:53,600
what I'm trying to say is,

91
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,740
if we're from different worlds,

92
00:05:55,879 --> 00:05:57,379
we'd be better off keeping our distance.

93
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,319
I know he's decent.

94
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:20,800
But somehow,

95
00:06:21,579 --> 00:06:22,600
I keep feeling like

96
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:24,060
we will always

97
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,459
travel on completely different paths.

98
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,899
We're from distinct worlds.

99
00:06:29,779 --> 00:06:31,500
How could we ever end up together?

100
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,720
Look at those gamblers downstairs.

101
00:06:40,959 --> 00:06:42,660
They think one lucky hand

102
00:06:42,759 --> 00:06:43,800
can beat the odds.

103
00:06:45,199 --> 00:06:46,279
But life...

104
00:06:46,839 --> 00:06:47,939
Life isn't as simple as

105
00:06:47,939 --> 00:06:48,860
a game of chance.

106
00:06:51,199 --> 00:06:52,300
Love, most of all.

107
00:06:53,639 --> 00:06:54,939
Once you lose that bet,

108
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,100
there's no comeback,

109
00:06:57,399 --> 00:06:58,560
no second chance.

110
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:25,860
Did you get burned?

111
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:27,699
No.

112
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:29,199
It's only warm water.

113
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:44,700
I'll drink it myself.

114
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,039
When did you get back?

115
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:13,379
A little while ago.

116
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:17,559
Have you had dinner?

117
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:18,500
Want me to

118
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:20,120
have the kitchen send something up?

119
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:21,759
No need.

120
00:09:38,399 --> 00:09:39,179
Your clothes are wet.

121
00:09:39,179 --> 00:09:40,139
I'll help you change.

122
00:09:41,559 --> 00:09:42,200
No, it's fine.

123
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,279
I can do it myself.

124
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:44,940
Your fingers are still stiff.

125
00:09:45,299 --> 00:09:45,960
Don't push it.

126
00:09:46,679 --> 00:09:47,740
I can have Tang

127
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:48,340
up here anytime.

128
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,960
Isn't it her time off?

129
00:09:59,419 --> 00:10:00,799
You used to go on about

130
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:02,179
everyone being born equal.

131
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,240
Now

132
00:10:03,899 --> 00:10:04,759
does that not apply

133
00:10:05,460 --> 00:10:06,899
to your own maid?

134
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,440
Does she deserve to toil away

135
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,480
around the clock for you?

136
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,080
Wh-what are you doing?

137
00:11:52,899 --> 00:11:54,039
If you need anything,

138
00:11:54,659 --> 00:11:55,399
just ring for me.

139
00:14:23,299 --> 00:14:24,500
It's cold and rainy outside.

140
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:26,600
Planning to freeze yourself out there?

141
00:14:52,639 --> 00:14:54,220
You're at headquarters all day,

142
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:56,240
handling military business.

143
00:14:56,759 --> 00:14:58,000
I'd feel guilty robbing you of

144
00:14:58,139 --> 00:14:59,460
a proper rest at night.

145
00:15:01,179 --> 00:15:02,740
What, am I just here for show?

146
00:15:24,179 --> 00:15:25,059
Want me sent for?

147
00:15:25,419 --> 00:15:26,080
Here's how.

148
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:30,720
One ring

149
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:32,679
means you want water.

150
00:15:42,299 --> 00:15:43,039
Two rings

151
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,399
means another blanket.

152
00:15:57,980 --> 00:15:59,120
And three rings?

153
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:03,240
Three...

154
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,379
means you miss me.

155
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:12,139
Got it?

156
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,899
Don't worry.

157
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,440
If you can't remember,

158
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,639
I'll teach you from scratch.

159
00:16:45,159 --> 00:16:46,039
What are you doing?

160
00:16:51,799 --> 00:16:53,240
You're seriously going to sleep here?

161
00:16:53,539 --> 00:16:55,139
Since you won't ring for me,

162
00:16:55,559 --> 00:16:56,259
I'll have to stay

163
00:16:56,259 --> 00:16:57,460
right by your side all night,

164
00:16:57,700 --> 00:16:58,620
at your beck and call.

165
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:00,399
You promised.

166
00:17:00,639 --> 00:17:01,659
We're not that close.

167
00:17:01,659 --> 00:17:02,220
Not enough

168
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:03,500
to share a bed!

169
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,819
Get out.

170
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,140
You said

171
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,359
if I rang the bell,

172
00:17:20,359 --> 00:17:21,819
you'd do as I asked.

173
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,579
Quick learner, huh?

174
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:28,319
Go sleep on your army cot.

175
00:17:32,599 --> 00:17:33,160
Off you go.

176
00:18:01,759 --> 00:18:02,539
Three rings

177
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,779
means you miss me.

178
00:18:41,619 --> 00:18:42,279
Sir.

179
00:18:42,819 --> 00:18:43,420
You're here.

180
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:52,920
What's the matter?

181
00:18:55,359 --> 00:18:57,460
Last time I came, it was still this number.

182
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,000
Why the sudden price hike?

183
00:18:59,539 --> 00:19:01,960
Good stuff's always in demand.

184
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:03,700
And the more people want it,

185
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:05,559
the pricier it gets.

186
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,740
Then give me five silver dollars' worth.

187
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:10,000
Not gonna happen.

188
00:19:11,599 --> 00:19:12,359
Come on.

189
00:19:32,099 --> 00:19:32,779
Miss Lan.

190
00:19:35,519 --> 00:19:36,180
Who are you?

191
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:37,680
Let go of me!

192
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:42,680
Tong Chunhai, at your service.

193
00:19:43,339 --> 00:19:45,339
You're a star, Miss Lan,

194
00:19:45,539 --> 00:19:46,880
shining through the country.

195
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,019
I'm just another face in the crowd.

196
00:19:49,019 --> 00:19:49,960
Of course you wouldn't know me.

197
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:54,460
But you'll recognize this.

198
00:19:55,099 --> 00:19:56,539
A little something for you,

199
00:19:56,539 --> 00:19:57,440
for our first meeting.

200
00:20:00,039 --> 00:20:01,460
I live on Laifu Alley,

201
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:02,900
in the Jiazi compound.

202
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:03,960
If you feel like

203
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:05,400
paying me a visit,

204
00:20:09,319 --> 00:20:10,400
I'll be waiting.

205
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:37,279
The kids

206
00:20:37,279 --> 00:20:38,460
are recovering nicely.

207
00:20:38,859 --> 00:20:40,240
You took such good care of them.

208
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,759
The credit isn't mine.

209
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:44,519
You were the one who

210
00:20:44,519 --> 00:20:45,640
showed them all that patience.

211
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:47,180
They're willing to take their meds

212
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:48,359
only if you told them to.

213
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:51,900
Jinxuan, let me take you home.

214
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:52,680
It's fine.

215
00:20:52,779 --> 00:20:53,680
I can manage.

216
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,119
I'll hail a rickshaw, then.

217
00:20:55,299 --> 00:20:55,640
All right.

218
00:20:56,539 --> 00:20:57,240
Rickshaw!

219
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:07,359
I'm off.

220
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:08,180
Take care!

221
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:21,599
Put one row upright here.

222
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:22,740
Here, along this edge.

223
00:21:22,839 --> 00:21:23,920
Then connect it across.

224
00:21:26,279 --> 00:21:27,380
Line up the corner.

225
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:04,579
Let's get you up.

226
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:13,940
Breathe. You can do it.

227
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,119
All that meds and

228
00:22:16,119 --> 00:22:17,180
acupuncture from Dr. Dai

229
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:18,279
were done for a reason.

230
00:22:19,019 --> 00:22:19,819
And besides...

231
00:22:20,619 --> 00:22:21,599
you're the bravest person

232
00:22:21,599 --> 00:22:22,700
I've ever known.

233
00:22:24,839 --> 00:22:25,339
Give it a try.

234
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:28,839
I'll try.

235
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:04,440
Don't watch your feet.

236
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:05,079
Eyes forward.

237
00:23:10,839 --> 00:23:11,579
Beautiful.

238
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:13,279
Now the other foot.

239
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:14,599
That's it.

240
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:16,140
Easy does it.

241
00:23:19,119 --> 00:23:19,839
You're okay.

242
00:23:19,839 --> 00:23:21,019
I won't let you fall.

243
00:23:26,019 --> 00:23:27,460
We'll take it one step at a time.

244
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:28,480
See?

245
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:31,079
Your fingers were stiff at first,

246
00:23:31,740 --> 00:23:32,220
and now

247
00:23:32,220 --> 00:23:33,660
you thread beads like a pro.

248
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:36,940
We'll keep at it every day,

249
00:23:37,819 --> 00:23:39,220
and you'll only get better.

250
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:40,920
Okay?

251
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:44,339
Keep going.

252
00:23:53,519 --> 00:23:54,119
That's it.

253
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,019
Take it slow.

254
00:23:58,779 --> 00:23:59,880
You're improving already.

255
00:24:14,579 --> 00:24:15,059
Here.

256
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:16,119
Time for your medicine.

257
00:24:27,099 --> 00:24:27,720
Zongzi candy.

258
00:24:36,579 --> 00:24:37,440
Dr. Dai says

259
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:39,339
a hot spring soak can boost circulation

260
00:24:39,799 --> 00:24:40,700
and help ease

261
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,900
the aches from rehab.

262
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:06,460
You feel cold?

263
00:25:09,720 --> 00:25:10,220
Not at all.

264
00:25:13,319 --> 00:25:14,400
Dr. Dai says a massage

265
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:18,039
of the pressure points is a must

266
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:19,720
after exercising.

267
00:25:22,339 --> 00:25:23,039
Tell me if it hurts.

268
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:23,779
Does it hurt a lot?

269
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:26,819
Not really.

270
00:26:28,079 --> 00:26:28,759
I'm fine.

271
00:26:35,619 --> 00:26:36,559
Just tell me if it's too much.

272
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:38,119
Don't tough it out.

273
00:27:01,980 --> 00:27:03,000
Cover your eyes.

274
00:27:03,279 --> 00:27:04,900
It'll help you work on your balance.

275
00:27:07,819 --> 00:27:08,519
Try to relax.

276
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,160
Let go.

277
00:27:18,259 --> 00:27:19,160
I'll walk on my own.

278
00:27:20,079 --> 00:27:20,680
You sure?

279
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:03,759
I can walk!

280
00:28:08,420 --> 00:28:09,400
I can walk!

281
00:28:10,380 --> 00:28:11,099
Changxuan!

282
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:12,720
I can walk! I did it!

283
00:28:15,299 --> 00:28:16,039
Congrats.

284
00:28:18,660 --> 00:28:19,519
Thank you.

285
00:28:20,460 --> 00:28:21,759
Without you,

286
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,339
I don't know if I'd ever

287
00:28:23,339 --> 00:28:24,640
have woken up.

288
00:28:25,460 --> 00:28:26,400
Nor would I have had

289
00:28:26,579 --> 00:28:27,220
any idea that

290
00:28:27,220 --> 00:28:28,339
I'd be able to walk and run

291
00:28:28,339 --> 00:28:29,319
like everyone else again.

292
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:34,339
What do you want as a reward?

293
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,180
Anything you want.

294
00:28:40,980 --> 00:28:41,900
Those little zongzi candies.

295
00:28:55,279 --> 00:28:56,400
The evidence is all here.

296
00:28:57,059 --> 00:28:57,539
Now confess.

297
00:28:58,480 --> 00:29:00,279
Who was that inside man of yours,

298
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:02,539
passing off defective guns as good ones,

299
00:29:02,640 --> 00:29:03,640
smuggling them into the army?

300
00:29:45,740 --> 00:29:46,359
I've got your family

301
00:29:46,359 --> 00:29:47,519
settled outside the city.

302
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:49,380
They're out of danger for now.

303
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:52,480
But that depends.

304
00:29:55,480 --> 00:29:57,200
On how much you're willing to cooperate.

305
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:02,279
It was...

306
00:30:03,440 --> 00:30:05,519
a brigade commander in the 4th Army.

307
00:30:05,900 --> 00:30:06,299
Cai...

308
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:08,559
Cai Fuhu.

309
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:20,000
Ruitong,

310
00:30:20,839 --> 00:30:22,480
what do we do about Cai Fuhu?

311
00:30:22,579 --> 00:30:23,779
Should we tell Changxuan?

312
00:30:25,019 --> 00:30:26,279
Let's not bother him just yet.

313
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:28,359
Changxuan's helping Miss Ye recover.

314
00:30:28,559 --> 00:30:29,859
He should have some time with her.

315
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:31,160
Let's investigate

316
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:32,319
the evidence against Cai Fuhu

317
00:30:32,319 --> 00:30:33,500
then report back to him.

318
00:30:39,380 --> 00:30:41,099
You'll have to change how you address her.

319
00:30:42,019 --> 00:30:43,200
It's been almost two years

320
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,259
since they tied the knot.

321
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:45,619
She's been your sister-in-law for ages.

322
00:30:45,700 --> 00:30:47,119
Time you started calling her that.

323
00:30:50,579 --> 00:30:51,119
Come on.

324
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:21,519
Madam.

325
00:31:23,559 --> 00:31:24,619
I've found you some

326
00:31:24,619 --> 00:31:26,220
magazines and novels as you asked.

327
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:27,160
I hope there's

328
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:28,400
something that catches your eye.

329
00:31:28,579 --> 00:31:29,640
I'll go get you more.

330
00:31:36,079 --> 00:31:37,099
Just leave them here.

331
00:31:37,180 --> 00:31:38,180
I'll look through them later.

332
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:39,160
Thank you.

333
00:31:39,619 --> 00:31:41,180
I'll go see about some snacks.

334
00:32:39,519 --> 00:32:40,420
What are you reading?

335
00:32:42,099 --> 00:32:43,599
This author writes

336
00:32:43,599 --> 00:32:44,900
with such plainspoken sincerity.

337
00:32:45,059 --> 00:32:46,859
There's nothing flowery about the language,

338
00:32:46,859 --> 00:32:48,660
yet it has such grace and beauty.

339
00:32:48,859 --> 00:32:50,599
He writes about how fragile life is,

340
00:32:50,599 --> 00:32:51,559
but somehow,

341
00:32:51,559 --> 00:32:53,240
it still stirs the soul.

342
00:32:55,559 --> 00:32:57,859
If you like it, it must be good.

343
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:28,579
Who brought you these books?

344
00:33:30,779 --> 00:33:31,779
Tang did.

345
00:33:32,619 --> 00:33:33,420
Why do you ask?

346
00:33:35,519 --> 00:33:36,359
I have things to take care of.

347
00:33:37,599 --> 00:33:39,000
I'll be back at dinnertime.

348
00:33:52,900 --> 00:33:54,480
Did you hire this maid?

349
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:55,940
I did, sir.

350
00:33:56,660 --> 00:33:57,400
Did she...

351
00:33:57,599 --> 00:33:59,039
Did she do something wrong?

352
00:33:59,559 --> 00:34:00,539
We don't need her here anymore.

353
00:34:01,099 --> 00:34:02,160
Tell her to leave. Now.

354
00:34:04,259 --> 00:34:05,019
Sir...

355
00:34:05,099 --> 00:34:05,839
Please, I'm begging you.

356
00:34:05,880 --> 00:34:06,960
Don't throw me out.

357
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:08,699
Please don't send me away!

358
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:10,920
My father's a gambler.

359
00:34:11,119 --> 00:34:12,400
Nanny Zhao took pity on me,

360
00:34:12,539 --> 00:34:13,800
buying me out and kindly

361
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:14,699
getting me the job.

362
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:16,280
Madam has also been so kind to me.

363
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:17,679
I've done everything I can

364
00:34:17,679 --> 00:34:18,900
to take good care of her.

365
00:34:19,099 --> 00:34:19,820
Sir,

366
00:34:19,960 --> 00:34:20,840
I'm begging you.

367
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:21,940
Please don't send me away.

368
00:34:21,940 --> 00:34:23,460
Please. I'm begging you.

369
00:34:23,460 --> 00:34:25,519
Sir, please!

370
00:34:25,519 --> 00:34:26,960
Don't throw me out.

371
00:34:35,139 --> 00:34:35,880
Please!

372
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:37,960
Tang, get up.

373
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:52,960
Without my permission,

374
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:55,219
no one is sending her away.

375
00:35:09,340 --> 00:35:10,179
Come out. Now.

376
00:35:20,619 --> 00:35:21,659
Those magazines

377
00:35:22,139 --> 00:35:24,039
were my idea.

378
00:35:24,699 --> 00:35:26,000
I just wanted something to read.

379
00:35:26,300 --> 00:35:27,820
She had nothing to do with it.

380
00:35:29,780 --> 00:35:31,059
I can't get my head around

381
00:35:31,599 --> 00:35:32,760
how these magazines

382
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:33,820
possibly got on your nerves.

383
00:35:34,880 --> 00:35:36,500
They're subversive publications.

384
00:35:36,900 --> 00:35:38,460
They'll do you no good.

385
00:35:38,500 --> 00:35:39,019
So you think

386
00:35:39,019 --> 00:35:40,239
you can just sell a girl off on a whim?

387
00:35:40,239 --> 00:35:41,400
She did something wrong.

388
00:35:42,039 --> 00:35:43,500
Her stay at Redleaf is the cost.

389
00:35:51,039 --> 00:35:51,980
Why are you suddenly

390
00:35:51,980 --> 00:35:53,099
a different person?

391
00:36:01,559 --> 00:36:03,039
You've been good to me,

392
00:36:04,639 --> 00:36:05,760
but I'm not some possession

393
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,900
you can keep locked up here.

394
00:36:08,340 --> 00:36:09,420
If you can't treat me

395
00:36:09,420 --> 00:36:10,500
as an equal,

396
00:36:13,059 --> 00:36:13,980
I'll have to rethink

397
00:36:13,980 --> 00:36:15,519
what this relationship means to me.

398
00:36:38,199 --> 00:36:39,400
Whether Tang's staying or not,

399
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:42,460
I shall reconsider.

400
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:46,260
As for you and me,

401
00:36:48,360 --> 00:36:49,659
when it begins

402
00:36:51,300 --> 00:36:52,639
and when it ends,

403
00:36:55,300 --> 00:36:56,860
that's for me to decide.

404
00:37:32,820 --> 00:37:33,480
All right, all right.

405
00:37:33,519 --> 00:37:34,519
Enough, enough.

406
00:37:34,739 --> 00:37:36,300
Take it easy on the drinks.

407
00:37:37,719 --> 00:37:38,440
I'm telling you,

408
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:39,920
you can't just bark orders at her

409
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:41,000
like you're back

410
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:41,980
in the barracks,

411
00:37:41,980 --> 00:37:43,239
throwing your weight around.

412
00:37:43,460 --> 00:37:44,519
When you get back to Redleaf,

413
00:37:44,519 --> 00:37:45,679
try sweet-talking her a little.

414
00:37:45,679 --> 00:37:47,079
She'll come around.

415
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:49,840
From the very beginning,

416
00:37:52,619 --> 00:37:53,820
between us,

417
00:37:55,139 --> 00:37:55,579
it was as if

418
00:37:55,579 --> 00:37:57,039
there was an invisible wall.

419
00:38:02,079 --> 00:38:02,960
Funny thing is,

420
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,440
once I finally got close,

421
00:38:09,199 --> 00:38:10,860
the wall was still there.

422
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:12,400
If you ask me,

423
00:38:13,079 --> 00:38:14,219
some things are best

424
00:38:14,219 --> 00:38:15,880
talked through confidantes.

425
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:16,840
That's what works.

426
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:17,460
Right?

427
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:21,980
Maybe we could ask Miss Lan.

428
00:38:24,380 --> 00:38:25,639
She and our sister-in-law

429
00:38:25,639 --> 00:38:26,340
used to be close.

430
00:38:27,420 --> 00:38:29,239
Maybe they still click.

431
00:38:29,739 --> 00:38:30,380
You know what?

432
00:38:30,380 --> 00:38:31,780
Gu's actually onto something.

433
00:38:31,780 --> 00:38:32,679
Look who's finally catching on.

434
00:38:33,219 --> 00:38:33,659
Seriously.

435
00:38:33,940 --> 00:38:35,059
I'll bet Miss Lan can

436
00:38:35,059 --> 00:38:35,639
get through to her

437
00:38:35,639 --> 00:38:36,840
the way unimaginable by men.

438
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:37,320
Right?

439
00:38:46,239 --> 00:38:47,179
Why are you suddenly

440
00:38:47,179 --> 00:38:48,300
a different person?

441
00:38:56,780 --> 00:38:58,139
You've been good to me,

442
00:38:59,760 --> 00:39:00,880
but I'm not some possession

443
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:02,000
you can keep locked up here.

444
00:39:03,139 --> 00:39:04,179
If you can't treat me

445
00:39:04,179 --> 00:39:05,239
as an equal,

446
00:39:07,119 --> 00:39:08,079
I'll have to rethink

447
00:39:08,079 --> 00:39:09,679
what this relationship means to me.

448
00:39:12,840 --> 00:39:14,639
As for you and me,

449
00:39:15,940 --> 00:39:17,280
when it begins

450
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:20,199
and when it ends,

451
00:39:21,239 --> 00:39:22,739
that's for me to decide.

452
00:40:08,119 --> 00:40:10,179
What brings you here?

453
00:40:11,059 --> 00:40:12,420
It's been ages since you last came by.

454
00:40:13,260 --> 00:40:14,059
Miss Lan.

455
00:40:14,760 --> 00:40:15,659
There's something

456
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:17,360
I need your help with.

457
00:41:15,559 --> 00:41:16,460
Qing.

458
00:41:16,900 --> 00:41:18,500
You have such a lovely voice.

459
00:41:19,139 --> 00:41:21,760
Thanks for coming all this way to keep me company.

460
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:24,159
Pingjun,

461
00:41:25,659 --> 00:41:27,519
you really don't remember any of it?

462
00:41:32,179 --> 00:41:34,139
My time at the Grand Vernal

463
00:41:34,739 --> 00:41:36,559
is walled off from me somehow.

464
00:41:37,460 --> 00:41:39,400
But when I heard your voice just now,

465
00:41:40,119 --> 00:41:41,260
something about it

466
00:41:41,539 --> 00:41:43,139
felt oddly familiar.

467
00:41:53,940 --> 00:41:54,659
Look.

468
00:41:56,119 --> 00:41:58,079
You used to transcribe scripts for me.

469
00:41:58,539 --> 00:41:59,739
You'd read them aloud to me

470
00:42:00,760 --> 00:42:01,579
again and again,

471
00:42:01,579 --> 00:42:02,860
once you finished.

472
00:42:04,599 --> 00:42:05,400
Later on,

473
00:42:05,900 --> 00:42:07,280
you joined Spring Breeze Theatre,

474
00:42:07,519 --> 00:42:08,800
writing new-style plays.

475
00:42:09,260 --> 00:42:10,820
The progressive students

476
00:42:10,900 --> 00:42:12,480
and all the educated ladies and gentlemen

477
00:42:12,820 --> 00:42:14,280
couldn't stop singing your praises.

478
00:42:15,559 --> 00:42:16,420
In your plays,

479
00:42:16,539 --> 00:42:17,719
you wrote about

480
00:42:17,719 --> 00:42:19,400
saving our country and its people.

481
00:42:19,659 --> 00:42:21,659
You even wrote plays urging people to boycott Japanese goods.

482
00:42:23,760 --> 00:42:24,559
Pingjun,

483
00:42:25,199 --> 00:42:26,539
I truly admire you.

484
00:42:27,960 --> 00:42:29,460
What you've done

485
00:42:29,659 --> 00:42:31,500
is more than I could ever hope to do.

486
00:42:35,500 --> 00:42:36,440
Qing,

487
00:42:37,820 --> 00:42:38,719
thank you for telling me

488
00:42:38,719 --> 00:42:39,860
about my past.

489
00:42:42,860 --> 00:42:43,840
Miss Lan,

490
00:42:44,179 --> 00:42:44,900
it's all thanks to

491
00:42:44,900 --> 00:42:45,659
Madam here

492
00:42:45,659 --> 00:42:46,860
that I get to hear you perform.

493
00:42:47,119 --> 00:42:47,719
Madam,

494
00:42:47,719 --> 00:42:48,420
shall we take the medicine?

495
00:42:50,159 --> 00:42:51,659
Surely I don't have to take this

496
00:42:51,659 --> 00:42:52,900
with every single meal?

497
00:42:53,420 --> 00:42:54,420
Just put it aside for now.

498
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:56,320
Madam,

499
00:42:56,860 --> 00:42:58,579
The master foresees it all.

500
00:42:58,860 --> 00:43:00,480
He went to quite a few old-established shops

501
00:43:00,619 --> 00:43:01,900
to get you some pear syrup candy.

502
00:43:02,199 --> 00:43:03,360
Says it takes the bitterness right out.

503
00:43:37,860 --> 00:43:38,559
My dear,

504
00:43:39,119 --> 00:43:41,260
Master has been so thoughtful.

505
00:43:41,519 --> 00:43:43,599
It's plain how much you mean to him.

506
00:43:46,719 --> 00:43:48,159
I know he's good to me.

507
00:43:50,280 --> 00:43:52,079
But I can't shake the feeling

508
00:43:52,500 --> 00:43:53,519
that between us,

509
00:43:53,519 --> 00:43:54,780
there's something in the way.

510
00:43:59,920 --> 00:44:00,900
Don't worry.

511
00:44:01,960 --> 00:44:03,019
I've watched the two of you

512
00:44:03,019 --> 00:44:04,280
from the very beginning.

513
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:06,840
The first time I saw him look at you,

514
00:44:07,320 --> 00:44:08,320
I knew right away

515
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:10,820
you'd stolen his heart.

516
00:44:11,300 --> 00:44:12,679
Your joys and sorrows

517
00:44:13,019 --> 00:44:14,820
come first for him.

518
00:44:16,420 --> 00:44:17,500
Neither of you

519
00:44:18,340 --> 00:44:19,139
would think twice

520
00:44:20,619 --> 00:44:22,579
about laying down your life for the other.

521
00:44:27,519 --> 00:44:28,559
Still,

522
00:44:28,920 --> 00:44:30,719
when it comes to matters of the heart,

523
00:44:31,460 --> 00:44:33,119
outsiders can only say so much.

524
00:44:36,420 --> 00:44:37,920
As for you and Changxuan,

525
00:44:38,699 --> 00:44:42,559
you'll come to understand it for yourself, in time.

526
00:44:55,059 --> 00:44:56,219
Hope to see you again!

527
00:44:56,780 --> 00:44:57,559
Anytime.

528
00:44:57,559 --> 00:44:57,960
Sure!

529
00:44:59,159 --> 00:45:00,519
Take it easy.

530
00:45:00,559 --> 00:45:02,099
I'll be back tomorrow!

531
00:45:02,159 --> 00:45:03,019
See you then!

532
00:45:05,659 --> 00:45:06,380
Whose car is this?

533
00:45:06,659 --> 00:45:07,460
It's blocking the road!

534
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:09,159
Move the damn thing!

535
00:45:11,599 --> 00:45:12,400
Cai Fuhu.

536
00:45:18,679 --> 00:45:19,579
What do you think you're doing?

537
00:45:36,880 --> 00:45:37,679
Madam,

538
00:45:37,980 --> 00:45:39,320
the doctor says you are recovering

539
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:40,139
remarkably well.

540
00:45:42,340 --> 00:45:43,340
He also said

541
00:45:43,340 --> 00:45:44,820
you should keep moving.

542
00:45:45,079 --> 00:45:46,679
The master's temporary headquarters isn't far

543
00:45:46,679 --> 00:45:47,480
from Redleaf.

544
00:45:47,800 --> 00:45:49,480
There's a ginkgo-lined road outside,

545
00:45:49,820 --> 00:45:51,579
the leaves turning a gorgeous gold.

546
00:45:52,480 --> 00:45:53,780
Shall I take you out

547
00:45:53,900 --> 00:45:54,360
for a look?

548
00:45:56,480 --> 00:45:57,000
All right.

549
00:45:58,480 --> 00:45:58,719
Come on.

550
00:46:05,619 --> 00:46:06,320
I'm a fool!

551
00:46:06,679 --> 00:46:07,820
I'm so stupid!

552
00:46:08,039 --> 00:46:09,159
I'm a fool!

553
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:10,440
I... I deserved it!

554
00:46:10,500 --> 00:46:11,320
I'm such an asshole!

555
00:46:11,320 --> 00:46:12,239
Finished?

556
00:46:14,039 --> 00:46:15,119
Good. Now, down to business.

557
00:46:15,159 --> 00:46:15,780
General,

558
00:46:16,280 --> 00:46:17,360
I wasn't thinking straight.

559
00:46:17,440 --> 00:46:19,000
I just wanted to make a little extra money.

560
00:46:19,199 --> 00:46:20,559
Only a tiny fraction of those guns

561
00:46:20,559 --> 00:46:21,480
were swapped out for faulty ones.

562
00:46:21,659 --> 00:46:23,039
I've got parents to support and kids to raise.

563
00:46:23,139 --> 00:46:24,099
If I die,

564
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:25,460
how will they

565
00:46:25,460 --> 00:46:26,519
manage without me?

566
00:46:26,519 --> 00:46:27,639
I'm begging you...

567
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:30,800
That's easy for you to say.

568
00:46:31,599 --> 00:46:33,460
Do you realize your faulty guns

569
00:46:33,659 --> 00:46:34,840
nearly wiped out

570
00:46:34,840 --> 00:46:36,719
an entire squad?

571
00:46:46,659 --> 00:46:47,239
General.

572
00:46:47,780 --> 00:46:48,820
It's all my fault.

573
00:46:49,139 --> 00:46:49,880
My son

574
00:46:49,880 --> 00:46:51,340
just turned eighteen.

575
00:46:51,500 --> 00:46:52,440
Please, have mercy.

576
00:46:52,440 --> 00:46:53,739
Spare him.

577
00:46:54,480 --> 00:46:56,079
Your son is precious.

578
00:46:57,300 --> 00:46:59,059
Does that make other people's sons expendable?

579
00:47:00,300 --> 00:47:02,059
Your son has barely been in the army a year,

580
00:47:02,460 --> 00:47:03,980
and you've already dragged him into

581
00:47:03,980 --> 00:47:05,860
this vile racket,

582
00:47:06,599 --> 00:47:09,099
victimizing so many innocent soldiers.

583
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:10,360
Tell me,

584
00:47:12,360 --> 00:47:13,719
why should I spare him?

585
00:47:20,400 --> 00:47:21,199
Dad! Dad!

586
00:47:21,260 --> 00:47:22,059
I don't want to die!

587
00:47:22,219 --> 00:47:23,019
Save me, Dad!

588
00:47:23,019 --> 00:47:23,820
I don't want to die!

589
00:47:24,860 --> 00:47:25,599
General! General!

590
00:47:25,800 --> 00:47:26,760
Please, Mr. Yu!

591
00:47:26,820 --> 00:47:28,480
Commander Gu! Commander Gu!

592
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:30,719
Please, talk to Mr. Yu for mercy!

593
00:47:30,800 --> 00:47:32,559
I made one stupid mistake, that's all!

594
00:47:33,599 --> 00:47:34,300
General!

595
00:47:34,340 --> 00:47:34,980
General!

596
00:47:35,039 --> 00:47:36,480
Please, it's my first offense.

597
00:47:36,519 --> 00:47:37,380
I'm begging you,

598
00:47:37,380 --> 00:47:38,920
please spare our lives.

599
00:47:39,300 --> 00:47:41,000
Spare your lives?

600
00:47:42,400 --> 00:47:43,699
What about all those soldiers?

601
00:47:43,699 --> 00:47:45,059
No one spared them.

602
00:47:47,860 --> 00:47:48,159
General,

603
00:47:48,280 --> 00:47:49,900
I-I had nothing to do with this!

604
00:47:50,199 --> 00:47:51,159
My father made me do it!

605
00:47:51,159 --> 00:47:51,860
General! Please!

606
00:48:19,179 --> 00:48:20,960
Get these bastards out of here.
